<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!-- Standalone parent for the extracted qits-ci repo (docs/epics/qits-ci/ in the qits
         monorepo). The in-repo CI pipeline: a repository opts in by committing
         `.config/qits/ci-post-receive.yml`, qits-githost publishes an SCMPublishCommit for the
         push, ci reads the config back out of the pushed commit over the git host's content
         routes, runs each step's script in a fresh container, and records an advisory pass/fail
         per push.

         This context is HOST-SIDE by design and lives outside any workspace container: it starts
         one ephemeral step container per step on its own network — each running a qits-ci-daemon
         that dials back and executes the step as its own child — and GitConfigFetcher keeps its own
         bare git cache. qits-ci itself executes nothing. That is the boundary, not an accident of
         the monorepo.

         DELIBERATELY ITS OWN GAV, the qits-workspaces case rather than the qits-workspace-daemon
         one. The child directories are `ci` and `service`, generic names that would collide in the
         shared ~/.m2 (and the qits_shared_m2 volume every workspace container mounts) with the
         monorepo's own `eu.wohlben:ci` / `eu.wohlben:service`. So the coordinates are namespaced
         (`eu.wohlben.qits:qits-ci-*`) while the DIRECTORIES stay `ci/` and `service/` — the
         filtered git history is anchored to those paths and renaming them would sever it.

         Versions that must stay in step with qits (Quarkus platform, JDK release, MapStruct,
         Lombok) are duplicated here on purpose: a clone of THIS repo alone must build, with no
         monorepo and no parent to inherit from.

         Trimmed to what these two modules actually need. The monorepo's app-wide machinery is
         intentionally omitted: spotless, enforcer, the :8080 dev-mode port guard, isolated-test
         surefire chunking, the derive-fixture-bares antrun step, the maven build-cache extension,
         and the mandatory -Dqits.variant=oauth|forwardauth|local auth profiles. -->
    <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
    <artifactId>qits-ci</artifactId>
    <version>2026.829.212354</version>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>
    <name>qits-ci</name>

    <modules>
        <!-- Listed in dependency order for readability; Maven computes reactor order itself. -->
        <module>ci-daemon-protocol</module>
        <module>ci-events</module>
        <module>ci</module>
        <module>service</module>
    </modules>

    <properties>
        <qits.eventstream.version>2026.825.74539</qits.eventstream.version>
        <!-- qits-githost's event vocabulary: the SCM records a push announces. qits-ci consumes
             SCMPublishCommit and nothing else, but the jar is the whole vocabulary — it is a data
             module with one dependency (qits-eventstream) and no container.

             THE CUTOVER THE PREVIOUS COMMENT WAITED FOR HAS HAPPENED. This was 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT
             against a warning that "a build against the platform Maven repository cannot resolve a
             snapshot nobody published"; qits-githost released the jar on 2026-08-12 and this is that
             release. What kept the snapshot working until then was the bootstrap seed-publishing it
             into the registry, which is not a release and does not survive one being re-seeded. -->
        <qits.githost-events.version>2026.820.65553</qits.githost-events.version>
        <!-- qits-containers' client jar: the orchestrator qits-ci asks for every step container.
             Framework-free — one class, four answers, no arc and no OIDC extension — which is what
             lets service/ produce it as a bean in three lines.

             ALSO CUT OVER, on the same day and in this same commit: qits-containers released its
             client jar on 2026-08-12 and this is that release.

             HOW THE PAIR BIT, because the shape is what to remember rather than the two numbers.
             Both snapshots were seed-published into the registry by the bootstrap, so they resolved
             there for months; a salvage re-seeded the artifacts store without them, and every
             qits-ci build afterwards still passed because docker reused the cached maven layer —
             ten CACHED layers, including the one that resolves dependencies. The first source
             change since (2026.812.183516) invalidated that layer, resolved for real, and the
             release run died on both jars at once with "Could not find artifact … 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT".
             A pin that only a warm cache and a developer's ~/.m2 can satisfy is a red release
             waiting for whoever next edits a file. Pin released calver, or the pin is a guess. -->
        <qits.containers-client.version>2026.822.190148</qits.containers-client.version>
        <qits.auth-core.version>2026.817.175344</qits.auth-core.version>
        <!-- The platform's datasource resilience, released out of libs/qits-integrations-quarkus
             together with the two above, which is why the strings match: qits-db-core carries
             PatientPgDriver — the pool opens its connections through it, and a request is HELD
             while postgres comes back rather than failed — and qits-arch-rules carries the
             assertion that this service configured it. They move together, because the rule names
             the driver as a STRING: a driver that moved without the rule would pass a build it
             should fail. -->
        <qits.db-core.version>2026.817.175344</qits.db-core.version>
        <qits.arch-rules.version>2026.817.175344</qits.arch-rules.version>
        <!-- The user-story framework (test scope): TokenValidationBootstrapIT is written as a
             @UserStory, so a run of that IT also regenerates service/target/userstories/ — the
             story's documentation, network diagram included — OBSERVED rather than narrated, since
             this version is the one that dropped Interactions.happened. It carries its OWN version
             rather than riding the three above, because it is released out of libs/qits-userflows
             and not out of the qits-integrations-quarkus reactor. -->
        <qits.userflows.version>2026.829.201516</qits.userflows.version>
        <!-- The recording service mocks the same IT boots against (the generic MockService plus
             idp.MockIdp), released out of libs/qits-integrations-quarkus like qits-auth-core,
             qits-db-core and qits-arch-rules above — so the same-string policy applies the day this
             repo consumes a newer reactor, and until then it names the release the mock idp
             actually shipped in. -->
        <qits.service-mock.version>2026.829.201505</qits.service-mock.version>
        <qits.maven.repository.url>http://registry.dev.localhost:8080/artifacts/maven/maven</qits.maven.repository.url>
        <maven.compiler.release>25</maven.compiler.release>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <project.reporting.outputEncoding>UTF-8</project.reporting.outputEncoding>

        <quarkus.platform.artifact-id>quarkus-bom</quarkus.platform.artifact-id>
        <quarkus.platform.group-id>io.quarkus.platform</quarkus.platform.group-id>
        <quarkus.platform.version>3.34.6</quarkus.platform.version>

        <!-- Embedded PostgreSQL for the suites. Both stores this repo boots are postgres now — its
             own `ci` datasource and the qits-eventstream jar's `eventstream` outbox — so every test
             that starts a persistence unit runs against one, and the first rule here is still that
             a CLONE TESTS GREEN WITH NO DOCKER. That rules out Testcontainers and Quarkus dev
             services alike. Zonky resolves real postgres binaries as ordinary Maven artifacts and
             spawns them as a child process: a dependency, not a container.

             Two coordinates, on purpose. The BOM pins which POSTGRES the binaries are (18.4.0 — the
             tag the platform's own qits-oci-postgresql image is built from), the library version is
             the harness around them, and they move independently. Every architecture the suites may
             run on is named explicitly in the modules: the binaries are per-arch artifacts, and a
             missing one fails in the middle of a suite rather than during resolution. -->
        <zonky.embedded-postgres.version>2.2.2</zonky.embedded-postgres.version>
        <zonky.postgres-binaries.version>18.4.0</zonky.postgres-binaries.version>

        <compiler-plugin.version>3.15.0</compiler-plugin.version>
        <surefire-plugin.version>3.5.4</surefire-plugin.version>
        <failsafe-plugin.version>3.5.4</failsafe-plugin.version>
        <jandex-plugin.version>3.4.0</jandex-plugin.version>
        <lombok.version>1.18.38</lombok.version>
        <!-- Quinoa is a quarkiverse extension and is not in the platform BOM, so it carries its own
             version. Used by `service` only; see the dependency's comment there for why 2.8.2 and
             not the newer 2.8.3. -->
        <quinoa.version>2.8.2</quinoa.version>
        <lombok-mapstruct-binding.version>0.2.0</lombok-mapstruct-binding.version>
        <mapstruct.version>1.6.3</mapstruct.version>

        <!-- The docker-backed ITs (CiDaemonHandshakeIT, CiDaemonGateIT) need real docker, a real
             step image and a built qits-ci-daemon binary, none of which a fresh clone has. `mvn
             verify` must be green without them — the same default the monorepo and qits-workspaces
             carry. Run them with -DskipITs=false. `service`'s `native` profile also flips it, so a
             `-Dnative` build exercises the binary it just compiled instead of packaging it and
             asserting nothing. -->
        <skipITs>true</skipITs>

        <!-- JUnit tags failsafe must NOT run, empty by default so `-DskipITs=false` still means
             "run everything", which is what AGENTS.md documents. Only the `native` profile sets it,
             to `extended`: that build wants the @QuarkusIntegrationTest against the binary, and the
             docker-backed ITs — tagged `extended`, needing real docker AND a step container that can
             route back to the JVM — are infrastructure tests that have nothing to say about
             native-image and fail rather than skip on a plain WSL2 host. Excluding them there keeps
             the native gate about the binary; they are still run, unchanged, by -DskipITs=false. -->
        <qits.it.excluded-groups/>
        <!-- Surefire's @{argLine} has no value unless something (jacoco/quarkus) sets it. -->
        <argLine/>
    </properties>

    <dependencyManagement>
        <dependencies>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${quarkus.platform.group-id}</groupId>
                <artifactId>${quarkus.platform.artifact-id}</artifactId>
                <version>${quarkus.platform.version}</version>
                <type>pom</type>
                <scope>import</scope>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- Which postgres the embedded binaries ARE — 18.4.0, the tag the platform's own
                     qits-oci-postgresql image is built from, so the suites prove the lineage
                     against the engine it ships on. Imported as a BOM because the per-arch
                     artifacts the modules name are separate coordinates. -->
                <groupId>io.zonky.test.postgres</groupId>
                <artifactId>embedded-postgres-binaries-bom</artifactId>
                <version>${zonky.postgres-binaries.version}</version>
                <type>pom</type>
                <scope>import</scope>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>io.zonky.test</groupId>
                <artifactId>embedded-postgres</artifactId>
                <version>${zonky.embedded-postgres.version}</version>
                <scope>test</scope>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
                <version>${lombok.version}</version>
                <scope>provided</scope>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
                <artifactId>mapstruct</artifactId>
                <version>${mapstruct.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <!-- org.yaml:snakeyaml (CiConfigParser's SafeConstructor) is managed by the Quarkus
                 BOM, so it stays version-less in the child pom exactly as in the monorepo. -->
            <!-- The reactor's own modules, so `service` depends on them version-less. -->
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-ci-domain</artifactId>
                <version>${project.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-ci-daemon-protocol</artifactId>
                <version>${project.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-eventstream</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.eventstream.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-ci-events</artifactId>
                <version>${project.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-githost-events</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.githost-events.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-containers-client</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.containers-client.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-auth-core</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.auth-core.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- The platform's shared ArchUnit rules, test scope wherever entities live. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-arch-rules</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.arch-rules.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- PatientPgDriver, named by config and reached by no code, plus DbRetry, which
                     the read seams call. COMPILE scope since the second one arrived: a runtime-only
                     jar cannot be imported. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-db-core</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.db-core.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- Test scope at every declaration site, like qits-arch-rules. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-userflows</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.userflows.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <dependency>
                <!-- Test scope at every declaration site, like qits-arch-rules. -->
                <groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
                <artifactId>qits-service-mock</artifactId>
                <version>${qits.service-mock.version}</version>
            </dependency>
        </dependencies>
    </dependencyManagement>

    <repositories>
        <repository>
            <id>qits-maven</id>
            <url>${qits.maven.repository.url}</url>
        </repository>
    </repositories>

    <build>
        <pluginManagement>
            <plugins>
                <plugin>
                    <groupId>${quarkus.platform.group-id}</groupId>
                    <artifactId>quarkus-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${quarkus.platform.version}</version>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${compiler-plugin.version}</version>
                    <configuration>
                        <parameters>true</parameters>
                        <!-- Incremental compilation leaves stale MapStruct *Impl classes behind
                             when a mapper's shape changes; the monorepo disables it for the same
                             reason. -->
                        <useIncrementalCompilation>false</useIncrementalCompilation>
                        <annotationProcessorPaths>
                            <path>
                                <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                                <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
                                <version>${lombok.version}</version>
                            </path>
                            <path>
                                <groupId>org.mapstruct</groupId>
                                <artifactId>mapstruct-processor</artifactId>
                                <version>${mapstruct.version}</version>
                            </path>
                            <path>
                                <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                                <artifactId>lombok-mapstruct-binding</artifactId>
                                <version>${lombok-mapstruct-binding.version}</version>
                            </path>
                        </annotationProcessorPaths>
                    </configuration>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${surefire-plugin.version}</version>
                    <configuration>
                        <systemPropertyVariables>
                            <java.util.logging.manager>org.jboss.logmanager.LogManager</java.util.logging.manager>
                        </systemPropertyVariables>
                    </configuration>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <artifactId>maven-failsafe-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${failsafe-plugin.version}</version>
                </plugin>
                <plugin>
                    <groupId>io.smallrye</groupId>
                    <artifactId>jandex-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                    <version>${jandex-plugin.version}</version>
                    <executions>
                        <execution>
                            <id>make-index</id>
                            <goals>
                                <goal>jandex</goal>
                            </goals>
                        </execution>
                    </executions>
                </plugin>
            </plugins>
        </pluginManagement>
    </build>
</project>
